body:
Adding the `updating` flag certainly prevents crashes, but the warning is incorrect.

It is actually possible to modify AnimationPlayer's own `current_animation`. For example, setting `current_animation` to `Animation2` at the end of `Animation1` is valid.

The actual issue only occurs when `set_current_animation()` calls a `stop()`. So this PR supersedes/closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98704 and closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98076.

This occurs when an empty string or the string “[stop]” is set to `current_animation` by the animation track (ValueTrack/MethodTrack/AnimationPlaybackTrack) during an animation.

Ideally, fixing the `stop()` process would allow stopping via `set_current_animation()` and eliminate the need for warnings.

However, if we prioritize preventing crashes by adding a warning, it should state something like: “You cannot stop AnimationPlayer by changing `current_animation` within the animation.”

```cpp
void AnimationPlayer::set_current_animation(const StringName &p_animation) {
	updating = true;
	if (p_animation == SNAME("[stop]") || p_animation.is_empty()) {
		if (updating) {
			updating = false;
			ERR_FAIL_EDMSG("You cannot stop AnimationPlayer by changing current_animation within the animation.");
		}
```
